WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.175
Today we light the top of the ladder: the broken and the busy.

2
00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:06.050
Remember them?

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.525
Not under command, and restricted in her ability to maneuver.

4
00:00:10.775 --> 00:00:14.675
Rule twenty-seven gives each a signal you can’t mistake.

5
00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:20.125
A vessel not under command shows two all-round red lights in a vertical line.

6
00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:22.375
By day, two balls.

7
00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:25.325
Red over red, the captain is dead.

8
00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:28.750
It’s a grim little rhyme, but you won’t forget it.

9
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.825
In this picture she isn’t making way, so the two red lights are all she shows.

10
00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:37.975
When she is making way, she adds sidelights and a sternlight.

11
00:00:38.225 --> 00:00:40.200
But no masthead light.

12
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:48.425
A vessel restricted in her ability to maneuver shows three all-round lights in a vertical line: red, white, red.

13
00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:51.575
By day, a ball, a diamond, and a ball.

14
00:00:51.825 --> 00:00:56.750
When she’s making way, she adds masthead lights, sidelights and a sternlight.

15
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.400
And at anchor, she shows her restricted lights plus her anchor lights.

16
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.825
So here’s how to read any of these.

17
00:01:05.075 --> 00:01:07.750
The special lights tell you her condition.

18
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.025
The ordinary lights tell you whether she’s moving.
